Construct a C program that not only outputs the quantity of command-line arguments provided when the program is executed, but also figures out the longest argument in terms of character length, the shortest argument and the sum of the lengths of all arguments. Also ensure that the program considers error handling for no arguments provided.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
    // Your implementation here
    return 0;
}
