```python
def partition(lst, low, high):
    """Partition the list in-place and return the index of the pivot."""
    pivot = lst[high]
    i = low - 1

    for j in range(low, high):
        if lst[j] < pivot:
            i += 1
            lst[i], lst[j] = lst[j], lst[i]

    lst[i+1], lst[high] = lst[high], lst[i+1]
    return i + 1


def quickselect(lst, k, low=None, high=None):
    """Return the k-th smallest element of lst. lst is modified."""
    if low is None: low = 0
    if high is None: high = len(lst) - 1
    pivot = partition(lst, low, high)
    if pivot == k:
        return lst[k]
    elif pivot > k:
        return quickselect(lst, k, low, pivot-1)
    else:
        return quickselect(lst, k, pivot+1, high)


def median(lst):
    n = len(lst)
    if n % 2 == 1:
        return quickselect(lst, n // 2)
    else:
        return (quickselect(lst, n // 2 - 1) + quickselect(lst, n // 2)) / 2
```
This partition function takes a list and two indices, and rearranges the list so that every element less than a certain pivot is on the left of the pivot in the list and every element greater is on the right, and then returns the index of the pivot.

The quickselect function takes a list, an index k, two optional indices, and uses the partition function to rearrange the list so that the kth smallest element of the list is in its correct, kth place.

The median function takes a list, and if the list has an odd length, it returns the middle element; otherwise, it returns the average of the two middle elements.

