answer:
The faulty code given doesn't initialize the root of the Trie. Consequently, it throws a NullPointerException when attempting to insert a string. Furthermore, the code within the insert method attempts to call a non-existing method "node()", when it should be creating a new TrieNode. The delete method of Trie only marks the node as not end of word but doesn't remove the key indeed. The code is not totally correct for the removal operation and doesn't function for some corner cases.

Here is the correct and optimized code for insertion, deletion, and retrieval in a Trie:

```java
class TrieNode {
    TrieNode[] children = new TrieNode[26];
    boolean isEndOfWord;

    public TrieNode() {
        isEndOfWord = false;
        for(int i = 0; i < 26; i++)
            children[i] = null;
    }
}

class Trie {
    private TrieNode root;

    public Trie() {
        root = new TrieNode();
    }


    void insert(String key) {
        if (key == null || key.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Input key is invalid");
        }

        TrieNode pNode = root;

        for(int level = 0; level < key.length(); level++) {
            int index = key.charAt(level) - 'a';

            if(index < 0 || index >= 26) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Input key contains invalid character: " + key.charAt(level));
            }

            if(pNode.children[index] == null)
                pNode.children[index] = new TrieNode();

            pNode = pNode.children[index];
        }

        pNode.isEndOfWord = true;
    }


    boolean delete(String key) {
        if (key == null || key.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Input key is invalid");
        }

        return delete(root, key, 0);
    }


    boolean delete(TrieNode node, String key, int index) {
        if (index == key.length()) {
            if (!node.isEndOfWord) {
                return false;
            }

            node.isEndOfWord = false;

            for (int i = 0; i < 26; i++) {
                if (node.children[i] != null) {
                    return false;
                }
            }

            return true;
        }

        int charIndex = key.charAt(index) - 'a';

        if(node.children[charIndex] == null || !delete(node.children[charIndex], key, index + 1)) {
            return false;
        }

        node.children[charIndex] = null;

        for (int i = 0; i < 26; i++) {
            if (node.children[i] != null) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;
    }
}
```
The given Trie supports insertion, deletion, and search operation for a set of strings. Please note that it only allows lower-case alphabet characters in the strings.

